# 0073-long-context-prefill: a prompt pass runs up to 4,096 rows above position 8,192, on a 2,048-row resume grid,
# with the gate/indexer fp32 GEMMs split at 2,048 rows, host row tables for passes up to 8,192, the Engram read-ahead
# sized by the next pass, and (TF_DS_PROMPT_ALIAS=1) the prompt pass's large scratch in five shared regions.
#
# Ported from BertholomusAI's two-node branch deepseek-v41-zig-tp2 (v0.7.1-v0.7.5): 3bb1d042d (chunk_rows 4096),
# 6456bf12d (fp32 GEMMs split at 2048), 42bcdeb97 (host row tables 8192), 1ec959ee0 (resume points on the 2048 grid),
# 37b7d2651 (TF_DS_PASS_ROWS/TF_DS_PASS_FROM, 2048 below 8192), 3befde133 (Engram read-ahead sized by the next pass),
# bfa786f42 (a stepped pass runs on while nothing else waits), 3b902fd21 (TF_DS_PROMPT_ALIAS). Their measurements on
# a two-Spark pair: prompt 93,335 tokens 2,136 -> 2,355 tok/s (+10%), 128K 2,428 -> 2,547 (+5%); TF_DS_PROMPT_ALIAS
# 1.9 GiB a node of prompt scratch instead of 4.6 (the 2,048-row build's 2.5). Not run on a pair in this recipe.
#
# The recipe's own choices: the spill tier's block size stays the 2,048-row resume grid (model.resume_rows), so the
# existing 2,048-row store and its fingerprint are kept; the extents stay aligned to the 4,096-row chunk (chunk_rows),
# as the tp2 branch has them. At CONTEXT=1,048,576 and MAX_TOKENS=65,536 a full-window request reserves 1,118,208
# positions (aligned to 4,096), so two fit in POOL >= 2,236,416; the recipe's 2,232,320 (aligned to 2,048) holds one.
# With TF_DS_PROMPT_ALIAS=1 and TF_DS_PASS_ROWS=4096 the 4,096-row scratch fits the arena; without the alias it is
# ~4.6 GiB and may not. TF_DS_PASS_ROWS=2048 keeps the 2,048-row passes, but the chunk's scratch is still sized for
# 4,096 rows; the alias is the way to make that fit.
#
# Switches: TF_DS_PASS_ROWS=N (a multiple of 2,048 from 2,048 to 4,096; unset 4,096), TF_DS_PASS_FROM=P (a position;
# unset 8,192), TF_DS_PROMPT_ALIAS=1 (off; TP2 only). The ranks need not agree on TF_DS_PROMPT_ALIAS (a rank's own
# memory); TF_DS_PASS_ROWS/TF_DS_PASS_FROM are rank 0's pass rule, the follower reads the frames.
#
